86603966}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa8dbe30-e720-5dad-94a3-94d991693f04" :question/math-academy-id "q-317037" :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is $T=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\,\\,$  \n      </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">\n        {{field-1}}\n      </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n        {{field-2}}\n      </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector $\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4x+6y \\\\ -7x+3y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4x+6y \\\\ -7x+3y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}]}
